          "r14"
        ]
      },
      {
        "finding": "Enhancing one value shifted non-target values (e.g., Creativity rose and Privacy fell in GPT-4.1).",
        "proposed_claim": "Value interventions spill over to correlated values.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r15",
          "r16",
          "r17"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "controls": "y",
    "capability_check": "y",
    "uncertainty_reported": "y",
    "code_released": "not stated",
    "peer_reviewed": "Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics",
    "problems": "The measured outcome is relative value ranking in forced-choice dilemmas, not safety refusal or harmful-request compliance. The authors note that Elo rankings reflect relative rather than absolute value priority, and that the causal basis of value correlations remains unclear.",
    "rows_left_out": "Not all model-by-strategy results in Figure 5 and the appendix were extracted; the aggregate strategy means and explicit textual examples were retained. Figure-only detailed rankings and entrenchment plots were left out because they do not measure the claim versions' safety outcomes.",
